diff --git a/UnitsNet.Modular/README.md b/UnitsNet.Modular/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ab0c66e30fe2ef11f1ab3f22c76e51faad021673
--- /dev/null
+++ b/UnitsNet.Modular/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# UnitsNet.Modular
+
+UnitsNet.Modular generates consumer-owned quantity types from the quantities selected by a module. Reference the combined UnitsNet.Modular package, or reference its runtime project and its generator project as an MSBuild analyzer. The generated quantities do not require a reference to the main UnitsNet assembly.
+
+## Module declaration
+
+Declare one interface annotated with `UnitsNetModule` in each consumer compilation. Compose its selections through `IInclude<TSpec>` and `IIncludeProfile<TProfile>`.
+
+```csharp
+using UnitsNet.Modular;
+
+[QuantitySpec("UnitsNet.Length")]
+internal interface DistanceSpec;
+
+[UnitsNetModule]
+internal interface ApplicationUnits : IInclude<DistanceSpec>;
+```
+
+The consumer can then use `UnitsNet.Length.FromMeters(2.5).Centimeters`, which returns 250.
+
+## Select quantities
+
+Built-in marker names use the Spec suffix, such as `UnitsNet.Modular.BuiltIns.LengthSpec`. A user-defined marker with `QuantitySpec("UnitsNet.Length")` selects the same semantic definition, independently of the marker's C# name. Compose related selections with include profiles.
+
+## Filter units
+
+Use a unit-set marker and `IInclude<TSpec, TUnitSet>` to select units with the patterns declared by its `UnitSet` attribute. An invalid pattern or a selection that matches no units is diagnosed during compilation.
+
+## Quantity definition JSON
+
+Additional quantity definition files use the `.unitsnet.json` extension. Define a stable semantic ID, generated name, base unit and valid conversion expressions. A definition must contain its declared base unit. The samples under `Samples` contain complete custom definition files.
+
+## Register a definition
+
+Add custom definition files as analyzer additional files. Reuse a stable semantic ID across markers and definitions; duplicate definition IDs are diagnosed rather than selected by file order.
+
+## Add quantity relationships
+
+Additional relationship files use the `.unitsnet.relations.json` extension. Select all quantities required by a relationship and provide a valid relation definition. Generation diagnoses invalid relations and ambiguous generated targets.
+
+## Arithmetic and relationships
+
+Generated quantities support their declared arithmetic and relationships. Affine quantities require their associated offset quantity in the selected module. Independent quantities can use their own unit choices without changing global configuration.
+
+## Namespaces
+
+Generated quantity types belong to the consumer assembly under the UnitsNet namespaces. Do not reference the legacy UnitsNet package in that same consumer compilation, because it also declares those types. The generator reports this conflict.
+
+## Building and packaging
+
+Build the runtime and generator from the repository source. Pack `UnitsNet.Modular/UnitsNet.Modular.csproj` to produce the combined runtime, analyzer and transitive build assets. The standalone generator project is an internal build input. The combined package includes this README, `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` and the upstream .NET notice file.
+
+The project declares net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 runtime targets and a netstandard2.0 analyzer. Test a consuming application after packaging so that analyzer registration and dependencies are exercised through MSBuild.
